\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Not what these hands have done,
\par Can save this guilty soul;
\par Not what this toilings flesh has borne 
\par Can make my spirit whole.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Not what I feel or do
\par Can give me peace with God;
\par Not all my prayers, and sighs, and tears
\par Can bear my awful load.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Thy work alone, O Christ,
\par Can ease this weight of sin;
\par Thy blood alone, O Lamb of God;
\par Can give me peace within.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Thy love to me, O God,
\par Not mine, O Lord, to Thee,
\par Can rid me of this dark unrest,
\par And set my spirit free.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Thy grace alone, O God,
\par To me can pardon speak;
\par Thy power alone, O Son of God,
\par Can this sore bondage break.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. I bless the Christ of God,
\par I rest on love divine,
\par And with unfaltering lip and heart,
\par I call this Saviour mine.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

